AGENT QUICKSTART - READ, ACT, VERIFY

PicoNIX is not Linux. First call get_manual({}) to discover topics,
then read the smallest relevant page. Use help CMD for syntax.

READ-ONLY DISCOVERY
  execute_command({command:'ps'})
  execute_command({command:'ls /tmp'})
  execute_command({command:'cat /proc/memory'})
  execute_command({command:'pins'})
  get_manual({topic:'command-reference'})

CHOOSE THE INTERFACE
  Short noninteractive shell command -> execute_command
  Generate a /tmp/NAME text file    -> write_file (overwrites)
  Interactive app or terminal      -> terminal_read FIRST,
                                      then terminal_send
  Programming subset              -> languages/c, languages/asm,
                                      languages/python
  Existing task procedure         -> workflows
  Troubleshooting                 -> debug-checklist
  Tool limits / errors            -> mcp-workflow, safety-recovery

LIMITS
  execute_command: 119 ASCII bytes, 4096 output bytes,
  about 3 seconds. No persistent cwd and no interactive stdin.
  One PTY shell starts with mcpd and consumes a task slot.
  Six process slots total. Do not run indefinite readers.
  If an action fails or a reply is interrupted, inspect state
  before retrying; never blindly repeat writes or keypresses.

SAFETY
  Isolated trusted network only: MCP has no authentication/TLS.
  Seek authorization before destructive changes or device writes.
  Confirm success from observed output or state, not acceptance.
